## AI Chatbot for IAM (Ver. 0.1)

### Phase 1 : Delivery of 1st POC (Gen AI Chatbot) & Prep Phase 2

#### Week 1-2 :

- Paris Team + UAC Opeations (PM & SME) :
    - 1st **UAT** to score the accuracy of RAG-generated responses + feedbacks.
    - Provide edge cases to strengthen the model’s robustness (Delphine, Abire, Roméo)
    - Update/Complete the Knowledge Base.
    - Define specific User Stories for the phase 2 (read-only scope) (e.g. “As a manager, I want to check the status of my team’s permission request.”)
- Innovation Lab :
    - Optimize Prompt Engineering based on UAT feedback.
    - Fine-tune RAG retrieval parameters.
- Dev Team :
    - Identify existing APIs within MyIAM (Request Status, User Permission)
    - Prepare the architecture
    - Define the endpoint APIs (read-only) for the phase 2

#### Week 3-4 :

- Paris Team + UAC :
    - RAG 2.0 UAT + feedbacks
    - Define specific User Stories for the phase 2 (read-only scope) (e.g. As a manager, I want to check the status of my team’s permission request.)
- Innovation Lab :
    - Release the improved version of the RAG : RAG 2.0
    - Optimize and fine-tune the RAG 2.0 based on UAT feedbacks.
    - Begin research on integrating **Agentic Logic (Function Calling)** into the chatbot to facilitate seamless API interaction.
- Dev Team :
    - Develop the endpoint APIs  (read-only) for the phase 2 (ensure APIs meet the formatting requirements for the chabot).

#### Week 5-6 :

- Whole Team :
    - Final GenAI POC Evaluation → Has the RAG performance met the threshold for production release?
- Dev Team :
    - Complete development of the first batch of **Read-only API Endpoints** and deploy them to the Sandbox environment.
    - Conduct API Security Testing to ensure the AI chatbot only accesses data within authorized scopes.
    - Release of 1st POC Gen AI (deployment into MyIAM).
- Innovation Lab :
    - Release of 1st POC Gen AI.
    - Begin research on integrating **Agentic Logic (Function Calling)** into the chatbot to facilitate seamless API interaction.

### Phase 2 : Delivery of 2nd POC (read-only Agentic AI Chatbot) & Prep Phase 3

#### Week 7-8 :

- Paris Team + UAC :
    - Define data privacy boundaries (who can access to what).
    - Design the **Fallback Strategy**. Define how the Chatbot should politely respond to API timeouts or errors without exposing technical error codes to the user. e.g.
    
    If the API fails, the bot shouldn't just say "Error 500"; it should say something like:
    
    > *"I'm having trouble reaching the MyIAM system right now. You can check your status manually [here], or I can try again in a few minutes."*
    > 
- Dev Team :
    - Deliver the first batch of core Endpoints (e.g., `GET /request-status` and `GET /user-access`).
    - Implement **OAuth2 or API Key authentication** mechanisms to ensure the Chatbot accesses data strictly via the user’s own identity/permissions.
- Innovation Lab :
    - Integrate **Function Calling** (Agentic logic) within the Chatbot framework.
    - Build **API Response Templates** to transform raw JSON data into human-readable dialogue (e.g., converting `{status: 2}` into *"Your application is currently at Level 2 Approval"*).

#### Week 9-10 :

- Paris Team + UAC :
    - Design the frontend of chatbot.
- Dev Team :
    - Conduct UAT : Validate that real-time data returned by the AI matches the MyIAM web portal with 100% parity.
- Innovation Lab :
    - Handle **Multi-turn Dialogue Queries**. Ensure the AI maintains context (e.g., if a user asks *"What is my request status?"* followed by *"And what about my team?"*, the AI retains the previous intent).

#### **Week 11-12 :**

- Dev Team :
    - Conduct Load/Stress Testing : ensure MyIAM backend APIs can handle concurrent requests (e.g., 500 managers querying team permissions simultaneously).
- Whole Team :
    - Lauch the 1st POC (Beta Pilot) for a selected department.
    - UAT of the POC.
    - Collect feedbacks for phase 2.

#### Week 13-14 :

- Innovation Lab :
    - Optimize and fine-tune the POC based on UAT feedbacks.
- Dev Team :
    - Release of the read-only Agent AI chatbot (deployment into MyIAM).
